course: dictionary
lesson: 11803
title: The word bestowal
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A bestowal is the act of giving something special to someone, such as an honour, a gift or a title. It is a formal word, so you will meet it mostly in stories, speeches and ceremonies. «The king's bestowal of a medal surprised the whole village.» The king gave a medal, so bestowal means the giving.
explain: Use the clues around the word to check. Kings, medals and ceremonies tell you this is a special occasion, and the bestowal is the moment the honour is given. Ask yourself: what is being given? If it is an honour, a gift or a title, you have found the meaning.
explain: Try the swap test. «The mayor will make the bestowal of the key to the city at noon.» Put in the word giving: the mayor will make the giving of the key to the city at noon. It still makes sense, so bestowal means giving.
fact: A bestowal is the act of giving something, such as an honour, gift or title.
fact: «Bestowal» is a formal word, so it is used more in speeches, stories and ceremonies than in everyday talk.
fact: «The bestowal of an honour» means the giving of an honour to someone.
fact: You can say a bestowal or bestowals when you mean one or more acts of giving, and also use the word on its own when you mean the act in general.
exercise: What does bestowal mean? | *The act of giving something special to someone | Taking something away from someone | Running very fast in a race | A small wooden boat
exercise: «The bestowal of the award took place in the school hall.» What took place in the school hall? | A test in maths | A big family lunch | *The giving of an award | A game of football
exercise: Which word is the noun for giving an honour? | bestow | bestowed | *bestowal | barely
test: «The bestowal of a medal happened at noon.» What does bestowal mean here? | *The act of giving a medal | Lost property | Standing in a long line | A type of tree
test: Which sentence shows a bestowal? | *The queen gave the nurse a special honour for her bravery | It rained all afternoon | The bus was late again | The dog ran across the park
exam: «The bestowal of the title made her smile.» Which word could replace bestowal without changing the meaning? | hiding | forgetting | *giving | losing
